refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
boolsocket_connect Socketsocket stringaddress intnullport&null;
Initiate a connection to address using the Socket instance socket, which must be Socket instance created with socket_create.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
&return.success; The error code can be retrieved with socket_last_error. This code may be passed to socket_strerror to get a textual explanation of the error.
If the socket is non-blocking and the connection cannot be completed at once, as is usual for TCP, this function returns &false; with the error Operation now in progress (SOCKET_EINPROGRESS), without any warning. A connection of a datagram socket, or to a local AF_UNIX socket, is usually completed at once. To finish a pending connection, wait for the socket to become writable with socket_select, then read the SO_ERROR option with socket_get_option: it is 0 when the connection succeeded.
